 aria-label="Block value 148" style="background: rgb(148, 148, 148);"></button><button data-v-ca10c6a9="" type="button" tabindex="-1" class="" aria-label="Block value 148" style="background: rgb(148, 148, 148);"></button><button data-v-ca10c6a9="" type="button" tabindex="-1" class="" aria-label="Block value 155" style="background: rgb(155, 155, 155);"></button><button data-v-ca10c6a9="" type="button" tabindex="-1" class="" aria-label="Block value 155" style="background: rgb(155, 155, 155);"></button><button data-v-ca10c6a9="" type="button" tabindex="-1" class="" aria-label="Block value 155" style="background: rgb(155, 155, 155);"></button><button data-v-ca10c6a9="" type="button" tabindex="-1" class="" aria-label="Block value 155" style="background: rgb(155, 155, 155);"></button><button data-v-ca10c6a9="" type="button" tabindex="-1" class="" aria-label="Block value 253" style="background: rgb(253, 253, 253);"></button><button data-v-ca10c6a9="" type="button" tabindex="-1" class="" aria-label="Block value 253" style="background: rgb(253, 253, 253);"></button><button data-v-ca10c6a9="" type="button" tabindex="-1" class="" aria-label="Block value 253" style="background: rgb(253, 253, 253);"></button><button data-v-ca10c6a9="" type="button" tabindex="-1" class="" aria-label="Block value 253" style="background: rgb(253, 253, 253);"></button><button data-v-ca10c6a9="" type="button" tabindex="-1" class="" aria-label="Block value 254" style="background: rgb(254, 254, 254);"></button><button data-v-ca10c6a9="" type="button" tabindex="-1" class="" aria-label="Block value 254" style="background: rgb(254, 254, 254);"></button><button data-v-ca10c6a9="" type="button" tabindex="-1" class="" aria-label="Block value 254" style="background: rgb(254, 254, 254);"></button><button data-v-ca10c6a9="" type="button" tabindex="-1" class="" aria-label="Block value 254" style="background: rgb(254, 254, 254);"></button><button data-v-ca10c6a9="" type="button" tabindex="-1" class="" aria-label="Block value 148" style="background: rgb(148, 148, 148);"></button><button data-v-ca10c6a9="" type="button" tabindex="-1" class="" aria-label="Block value 148" style="background: rgb(148, 148, 148);"></button><button data-v-ca10c6a9="" type="button" tabindex="-1" class="" aria-label="Block value 148" style="background: rgb(148, 148, 148);"></button><button data-v-ca10c6a9="" type="button" tabindex="-1" class="" aria-label="Block value 148" style="background: rgb(148, 148, 148);"></button><button data-v-ca10c6a9="" type="button" tabindex="-1" class="" aria-label="Block value 155" style="background: rgb(155, 155, 155);"></button><button data-v-ca10c6a9="" type="button" tabindex="-1" class="" aria-label="Block value 155" style="background: rgb(155, 155, 155);"></button><button data-v-ca10c6a9="" type="button" tabindex="-1" class="" aria-label="Block value 155" style="background: rgb(155, 155, 155);"></button><button data-v-ca10c6a9="" type="button" tabindex="-1" class="" aria-label="Block value 155" style="background: rgb(155, 155, 155);"></button><button data-v-ca10c6a9="" type="button" tabindex="-1" class="" aria-label="Block value 253" style="background: rgb(253, 253, 253);"></button><button data-v-ca10c6a9="" type="button" tabindex="-1" class="" aria-label="Block value 253" style="background: rgb(253, 253, 253);"></button><button data-v-ca10c6a9="" type="button" tabindex="-1" class="" aria-label="Block value 253" style="background: rgb(253, 253, 253);"></button><button data-v-ca10c6a9="" type="button" tabindex="-1" class="" aria-label="Block value 253" style="background: rgb(253, 253, 253);"></button></div></div></div><figcaption data-v-ca10c6a9="">Each block keeps one number: the mean brightness of the pixels inside it. At 8×8 the letter is four grey squares, but those four greys still differ from the four greys a "b" or "o" would produce, which is why small pixelated text can be matched by guessing.</figcaption></figure></section><section class="wrap block prose"><h2>Pixelate vs blur: which to use</h2><div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th></th><th>Pixelate</th><th>Blur</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Look</td><td>Obvious "censored" squares</td><td>Soft, less distracting</td></tr><tr><td>Faces in photos</td><td>Good at large block sizes</td><td>Good at high strength</td></tr><tr><td>Short text, numbers</td><td>Can be guessed back</td><td>Can be guessed back</td></tr><tr><td>Best for</td><td>Making it clear something was hidden on purpose</td><td>Keeping a screenshot pleasant to read</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>For anything that must never be read, switch to <a href="https://blurshot.io/redact-image" class="">solid-box redaction</a>.</p><h2>Tips for a clean pixelated result</h2><ul><li>Make the box a little bigger than the thing you are hiding. Edges of letters that fall just outside a block stay sharp.</li><li>Use bigger blocks on small details. A 10-pixel-tall line of text needs blocks at least as tall as the text.</li><li>For faces in group photos, <a href="https://blurshot.io/blur-face" class="">the face editor</a> can find every face for you, including the small ones at the back.</li></ul></section><div class="wrap"><section class="faq prose" aria-labelledby="faq-h"><h2 id="faq-h">Questions people ask</h2><details><summary>How do I pixelate only part of an image?</summary><p>Open the image, keep Pixelate selected and drag a box over the area. Each box keeps its own block size, so you can pixelate a face heavily and a background sign lightly in the same picture.</p></details><details><summary>How do I pixelate the whole image?</summary><p>Press "Whole image" after opening it. That adds one box covering every pixel, and the strength slider then sets the block size for the entire picture.</p></details><details><summary>What block size is enough?</summary><p>For faces, blocks about a fifth of the face width make it unrecognisable to people. For text, pixelation is never guaranteed: short strings in a known font can be guessed back. Use a solid box for numbers and passwords.</p></details><details><summary>Is pixelation the same as a mosaic effect?</summary><p>Yes. "Mosaic" is the name many photo apps use for the same block-averaging filter.</p></details><details><summary>Will the pixelated file still contain the original?</summary><p>No. The export is a new image drawn from the edited pixels, with no layers, undo history or metadata. Anyone receiving it gets only what you see.</p></details></section></div></div><!--]--></main><footer class="foot" data-v-a9d23265=""><div class="wrap foot-in" data-v-a9d23265=""><div data-v-a9d23265=""><p class="foot-brand" data-v-a9d23265="">Blur<span class="bar" data-v-a9d23265="">Shot</span></p><p data-v-a9d23265="">Blur, pixelate and redact screenshots in your browser. Nothing is uploaded unless you ask the optional AI finder for help.</p></div><nav aria-label="Guides" data-v-a9d23265=""><p class="foot-h" data-v-a9d23265="">Guides</p><a href="https://blurshot.io/how-to-redact-a-screenshot" class="" data-v-a9d23265="">How to redact a screenshot</a><a href="https://blurshot.io/unblur-image" class="" data-v-a9d23265="">Can blur be reversed?</a><a href="https://blurshot.io/remove-exif-data" class="" data-v-a9d23265="">Remove EXIF &amp; GPS</a><a href="https://blurshot.io/privacy" class="" data-v-a9d23265="">Privacy</a></nav></div></footer></div></div><div id="teleports"></div><script>window.__NUXT__={};window.__NUXT__.config={public:{},app:{baseURL:"/",buildId:"a0bc2086-2a0b-4616-a076-27adb4c0f2af",buildAssetsDir:"/_nuxt/",cdnURL:""}}</script><script type="application/json" data-nuxt-data="nuxt-app" data-ssr="true" id="__NUXT_DATA__" data-src="/_payload.json?_b=a0bc2086-2a0b-4616-a076-27adb4c0f2af">[{"state":1,"once":3,"_errors":4,"serverRendered":6,"path":7,"prerenderedAt":8},["Reactive",2],{},["Set"],["ShallowReactive",5],{},true,"\u002F",1790517776258]</script></body></html>